The JS code uses `arr[n+1] = []` and `arr[0] = []` then fills with dots for m+2 width. My PHP `array_fill` creates the full padded grid initially, then overwrites rows 1..n with actual data + side padding. This is cleaner.

The JS code reads line by line asynchronously. PHP is synchronous, so standard `fgets` loop works fine.

